mzn is a companion to RTK (Rust Token Killer), https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk,
Copyright 2024 rtk-ai and rtk-ai Labs, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. mzn does not include or redistribute RTK source code or binaries.
It invokes an RTK binary that the user installed separately, reads RTK's
local stats database read-only, and writes filter definitions in RTK's
documented TOML filter format. RTK's file formats, paths and command-line
behaviour were studied from its public source to stay compatible.

mzn can optionally detect Lerim, https://github.com/lerim-dev/lerim-cli,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. mzn does not include Lerim
code; it only checks for Lerim's presence and configuration.

Third-party Rust crates linked into the mzn binary are distributed under
their own licenses (MIT and/or Apache-2.0); see Cargo.lock for the list.
The binary embeds SQLite (public domain) via the rusqlite crate.
